   "notes": "The two 300 K elastic rows are retained separately. Table I visibly prints Cp=1.1288 at 300 K. That number breaks the smooth sequence and yields gamma=3.395 through Equation (12), whereas Table IV prints gamma=2.974. Equation (4) gives 1.28820 and inversion of Equation (12) with the printed Table III Ks and Table IV gamma gives 1.28843, so cp_reconstructed_0p1_j_g_k records 1.2888 as the evident intended value while preserving the literal print in the adjacent column. Low-temperature expansivities were obtained by graphical smoothing and are not independently reproducible from the article alone."
  },
